<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balaram Deva</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Balaram Dev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balaram Deva was a prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> ruling family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patna">Patna</a> State in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> who, according to tradition, founded a separate kingdom at Sambalpur on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahanadi">Mahanadi</a>. His kingdom soon became the leading power among the hill states of the region, known as the Garhjat. Sambalpur remained under his descendants until the British annexed it in 1849.</p></div>
